A biased four-sided die, $\mathrm{A}$, is rolled. Let $X$ be the score obtained when die $\mathrm{A}$ is rolled. The probability distribution for $X$ is given in the following table.
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|}
\hline$x$ & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\
\hline $\mathrm{P}(X=x)$ & $p$ & $p$ & $p$ & $\cfrac{1}{2} p$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
