explanation:
\section*{Section A}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item METHOD 1\\
recognition that $y=\int \cos \left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right) \mathrm{d} x$\\
$y=\sin \left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right)(+c)$\\
substitute both $x$ and $y$ values into their integrated expression including $c$\\
$2=\sin \frac{\pi}{2}+c$\\
$c=1$\\
$y=\sin \left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right)+1$
\end{enumerate}

\section*{METHOD 2}
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \int_{2}^{y} \mathrm{~d} y=\int_{\frac{3 \pi}{4}}^{x} \cos \left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right) \mathrm{d} x \\
& y-2=\sin \left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right)-\sin \frac{\pi}{2} \\
& y=\sin \left(x-\frac{\pi}{4}\right)+1
\end{aligned}
$$

