Question 12 continued.\\
(c) valid attempt to find $\omega_{1}-\omega_{3}$ (or $\omega_{3}-\omega_{1}$ )

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \omega_{1}-\omega_{3}=\left(1+\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}+\frac{1}{2} \mathrm{i}\right)-(1-\mathrm{i})=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}+\frac{3}{2} \mathrm{i} \text { OR } \cos \frac{\pi}{6}+\mathrm{i} \sin \frac{\pi}{6}+\mathrm{i} \sin \frac{\pi}{2} \\
& \text { valid attempt to find }\left|\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}+\frac{3}{2} \mathrm{i}\right| \\
& =\sqrt{\frac{3}{4}+\frac{9}{4}} \\
