The distances travelled by boat $\mathrm{A}$ and boat $\mathrm{B}$, after $t$ seconds, are $x$ metres and $y$ metres respectively. The angle $\theta$ is the radian measure of the bearing of boat $\mathrm{B}$ from boat $\mathrm{A}$. This information is shown on the following diagram.
