}

\begin{parts}
\part[1] Write down the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(1+t)^{-1}$ in ascending powers of $t$.
\part[4] By using the Maclaurin series for $\cos x$ and the result from part (a), show that the Maclaurin series for $\sec x$ up to and including the term in $x^4$ is $1+\cfrac{x^2}{2}+\cfrac{5 x^4}{24}$.
\part[3] By using the Maclaurin series for $\arctan x$ and the result from part (b), find $\lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(\cfrac{x \arctan 2 x}{\sec x-1}\right)$.
\end{parts}
}

explanation:
(a) $1-t+t^{2}$

Note: Accept $1,-t$ and $t^{2}$.\\
(b) $\sec x=\frac{1}{1-\frac{x^{2}}{2!}+\frac{x^{4}}{4!}(-\ldots)}\left(=\left(1-\frac{x^{2}}{2!}+\left(\frac{x^{4}}{4!}(-\ldots)\right)\right)^{-1}\right)$


\begin{equation*}
t=\cos x-1 \text { or } \sec x=1-(\cos x-1)+(\cos x-1)^{2} \tag{M1}
\end{equation*}


$$
\begin{aligned}
& =1-\left(-\frac{x^{2}}{2!}+\frac{x^{4}}{4!}(-\ldots)\right)+\left(-\frac{x^{2}}{2!}+\frac{x^{4}}{4!}(-\ldots)\right)^{2} \\
& =1+\frac{x^{2}}{2}-\frac{x^{4}}{24}+\frac{x^{4}}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$

so the Maclaurin series for $\sec x$ up to and including the term in $x^{4}$ is $1+\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\frac{5 x^{4}}{24} \quad$ AG

Note: Condone the absence of ' $\ldots$..\\
(c) $\arctan 2 x=2 x-\frac{(2 x)^{3}}{3}+\ldots$

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(\frac{x \arctan 2 x}{\sec x-1}\right)=\lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(\frac{x\left(2 x-\frac{(2 x)^{3}}{3}+\ldots\right)}{\left(1+\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\frac{5 x^{4}}{24}\right)-1}\right) \\
& =\lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(\frac{2 x^{2}-\frac{8 x^{4}}{3}+\ldots}{\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\frac{5 x^{4}}{24}}\right) \\
& =\lim _{x \rightarrow 0}\left(\frac{2 x^{2}\left(1-\frac{4 x^{2}}{3}\right)}{\frac{x^{2}}{2}\left(1+\frac{5 x^{2}}{12}\right)}\right) \\
& =4
\end{aligned}
$$

Note: Condone missing 'lim' and errors in higher derivatives.

question_text:
The flight times, $T$ minutes, between two cities can be modelled by a normal distribution with a mean of 75 minutes and a standard deviation of $\sigma$ minutes.
\begin{parts}
\part[3] Given that $2 \%$ of the flight times are longer than 82 minutes, find the value of $\sigma$.
\part[2] Find the probability that a randomly selected flight will have a flight time of more than 80 minutes.
\part[4] Given that a flight between the two cities takes longer than 80 minutes, find the probability that it takes less than 82 minutes.
On a particular day, there are 64 flights scheduled between these two cities.
\part[3] Find the expected number of flights that will have a flight time of more than 80 minutes.
\part[3] Find the probability that more than 6 of the flights on this particular day will have a flight time of more than 80 minutes.
\end{parts}
}

A function $f$ is defined by $f(x)=\cfrac{k \mathrm{e}^{\frac{x}{2}}}{1+\mathrm{e}^x}$ where $x \in \mathbb{R}, x \geq 0$ and $k \in \mathbb{R}^{+}$.
The region enclosed by the graph of $y=f(x)$, the $x$-axis, the $y$-axis and the line $x=\ln 16$ is rotated $360^{\circ}$ about the $x$-axis to form a solid of revolution.
\begin{parts}
\part[6] Show that the volume of the solid formed is $\cfrac{15 k^2 \pi}{34}$ cubic units.
